# 4) Find style and logic problems in this code

Given:

```java
public static Boolean isInvalid(Boolean value) {
    if (!value.equals(Boolean.FALSE)) {
        return true;
    } else {
        return false;
    }
}
```

Is code ko simple banaya ja sakta hai.

Actually:

```java
if (!value.equals(Boolean.FALSE))
```

ka direct meaning hai:

```java
value != false
```

So:

```java
public static Boolean isInvalid(Boolean value) {
    return !value.equals(Boolean.FALSE);
}
```

Aur better:

```java
public static boolean isInvalid(Boolean value) {
    return Boolean.TRUE.equals(value);
}
```

### Problem:

1. `if-else` unnecessary hai.
2. `Boolean` ki jagah primitive `boolean` use kar sakte hain.
3. `value.equals()` se `value == null` hua to `NullPointerException` aa sakta hai.

### Interview line:

> **The code has unnecessary if-else logic and can be simplified into a direct return statement. Also Boolean.TRUE.equals() is safer for null handling.**

