# 9) When does a Java object move from one heap generation to another?

Java heap generally generations me divided hota hai:

```text
Young Generation
      ↓
Old Generation
```

New objects generally **Young Generation** me create hote hain.

Agar object multiple Garbage Collections survive karta hai, to uski **age increase** hoti hai.

Enough GC cycles survive karne ke baad object:

```text
Young → Old
```

generation me promote ho sakta hai.

### Example:

```text
New Object
    ↓
Eden
    ↓
Survives GC
    ↓
Survivor
    ↓
Survives multiple GC
    ↓
Old Generation
```

### Interview line:

> **An object is initially allocated in the Young Generation. If it survives enough garbage collection cycles, it can be promoted to the Old Generation.**

**Remember:**

> `New → Young → Survive GC → Old`

