**Reliable code** means:

> **Aisa code jo expected situation me consistently sahi result de aur errors ko properly handle kare.**

Simple Hinglish me:

**Reliable = भरोसेमंद / dependable**

### Example:

Agar file read karne ka code hai:

```java
FileReader file = new FileReader("data.txt");
```

Agar `data.txt` exist nahi karti, program crash ho sakta hai.

Reliable code me hum exception handle karenge:

```java
try {
    FileReader file = new FileReader("data.txt");
} catch (IOException e) {
    System.out.println("File nahi mili");
}
```

Ab program unexpected way se crash hone ke bajay error ko properly handle karega.

### Interview me simple line:

> **Reliable code means code that consistently works as expected and properly handles possible errors or failures.**

**Yaad rakho:**
`Reliable = Correct + Consistent + Proper Error Handling`

=======================================================================================================
Haan 👍 **“survives”** ka simple meaning samjho.

### Survives = bach jaata hai

Garbage Collector (GC) ka kaam hai **unused objects ko delete karna**.

Example:

```java
Employee e = new Employee();
```

Ab `e` object memory me hai.

GC aaya aur check kiya:

```text
Kya koi object ko use/refer kar raha hai?
```

Agar **koi reference nahi hai**:

```text
Employee Object
      ↓
No reference
      ↓
GC delete kar dega ❌
```

Lekin agar reference abhi bhi hai:

```java
Employee e = new Employee();
```

to GC bolega:

```text
Employee Object
      ↑
      e
```

**"Is object ko abhi use kiya ja sakta hai, isko delete nahi karna."**

Ye object **GC se survive kar gaya**. ✅

---

### Multiple GC samjho

```text
Object created
      ↓
Young Generation
      ↓
GC aaya
      ↓
Object still being used
      ↓
SURVIVED ✅
      ↓
Next GC
      ↓
Still being used
      ↓
SURVIVED ✅
      ↓
Multiple GC survive
      ↓
Old Generation
```

### Ek real-life example 🏠

Socho school me teacher bolti hai:

> "Jis student ki attendance nahi hai, usko remove karo."

Student ki attendance hai → **student survive kar gaya**.

Next month phir checking hui → attendance hai → **phir survive**.

Aise multiple checks survive karne ke baad JVM object ko **Old Generation** me promote kar sakti hai.

### Bas ye yaad rakho:

> **Survive means GC ne object ko delete nahi kiya because object abhi bhi reachable/in-use tha.**

**GC aaya + object abhi bhi reachable hai = Object survived.**

