# Q5. How does designing a class help in developing an application?

Is question ka simple meaning hai:

> **Application banate time class ko kaise design karna chahiye, taaki code clean, reusable aur maintainable rahe?**

### Simple Answer:

Class design karte time hume ye cheezein follow karni chahiye:

### 1. Single Responsibility

Ek class ka **ek main kaam** hona chahiye.

❌ Wrong:

```java
class Employee {
    void calculateSalary() {}
    void saveToDatabase() {}
    void sendEmail() {}
}
```

Ek hi class 3 kaam kar rahi hai.

✅ Better:

```java
class SalaryService {
    void calculateSalary() {}
}

class EmployeeRepository {
    void saveToDatabase() {}
}

class EmailService {
    void sendEmail() {}
}
```

---

### 2. Reusability

Aisi class banao jise application ke multiple places par use kar sake.

### 3. Maintainability

Agar future me change karna ho, to easily change ho jaye aur poora application affect na ho.

### 4. Loose Coupling

Classes ek-dusre par unnecessarily dependent nahi honi chahiye.

### 5. Encapsulation

Data ko directly expose na karke methods ke through access karna.

```java
class Employee {

    private String name;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}
```

---

### 🎯 Interview me directly bolo:

> **Good class design helps us build applications that are reusable, maintainable, testable and loosely coupled. We should follow principles like Single Responsibility, Encapsulation and loose coupling.**

### 🧠 Yaad rakhne ka shortcut:

**Good Class =**

`SRP + Encapsulation + Loose Coupling + Reusability + Maintainability`

