# 🎯 Karat me agar pooche:

**"What is the design flaw?"**

Tum bolo:

> **The problem is that CarDealer contains type-specific logic using instanceof or type checking. This creates tight coupling and violates the Open/Closed Principle. If we add a new vehicle, we need to modify CarDealer. We can solve this using polymorphism by moving vehicle-specific behavior into the Vehicle implementations.**

### Aur agar interviewer pooche: **"Why is polymorphism better?"**

Bolo:

> **Because CarDealer only depends on the Vehicle abstraction. New vehicle types can be added without modifying CarDealer. This makes the code loosely coupled, extensible and easier to maintain.**

