## Q16. Convert this Runnable code into Lambda / Stream style

Pehle ek important correction: **Runnable ko Stream me convert nahi karte.** Runnable ko **Lambda expression** me convert karte hain. Agar question me actual code hai, usko lambda syntax me rewrite karna hai.

### Original Anonymous Class

```java
Runnable run = new Runnable() {
    @Override
    public void run() {
        System.out.println("Hello");
    }
};
```

### Lambda Version

```java
Runnable run = () -> {
    System.out.println("Hello");
};
```

Aur agar sirf ek statement hai, braces bhi hata sakte ho:

```java
Runnable run = () -> System.out.println("Hello");
```

### Why `()`?

Because `run()` method me **koi parameter nahi hai**:

```java
void run()
```

Isliye:

```java
() -> ...
```

### Agar parameter hota

Example:

```java
Consumer<String> c = (name) -> System.out.println(name);
```

Yahan `Consumer` ka method:

```java
void accept(String name)
```

Isliye:

```text
(String parameter) -> body
```

### 🧠 Karat me bolna:

> **Runnable is a functional interface because it has one abstract method, `run()`. Therefore, we can replace its anonymous class implementation with a lambda expression.**

**Shortcut:**

```text
No parameter → () ->
One parameter → x ->
Multiple parameters → (x, y) ->
```

