# Q19. What is `OutOfMemoryError` in Java?

Simple language me:

> **Jab JVM ke paas kisi new object ko store karne ke liye enough memory nahi bachti, tab `OutOfMemoryError` aa sakta hai.**

### Simple example

```java
List<int[]> list = new ArrayList<>();

while (true) {
    list.add(new int[1000000]);
}
```

Yahan hum continuously naye arrays bana rahe hain:

```text
Array 1 → Heap
Array 2 → Heap
Array 3 → Heap
Array 4 → Heap
...
Array 10000 → Heap
...
Memory full ❌
        ↓
OutOfMemoryError
```

### Important point

Java ka **Garbage Collector** memory clean karta hai.

Lekin agar objects abhi bhi reachable hain:

```java
list → object
```

to GC unko delete nahi karega.

Isliye memory continuously consume hoti rahegi.

---

## Common reasons

### 1. Bahut saare objects create karna

```java
while(true) {
    list.add(new Employee());
}
```

### 2. Memory leak

Object ki zarurat nahi hai, lekin reference abhi bhi maintained hai.

### 3. Heap size chhota hai

JVM ko limited heap memory mili hai.

### 4. Large objects

Bahut bade arrays/files/data memory me load karna.

---

## 🧠 Simple real-life example

Socho tumhare paas ek room hai:

```text
Room capacity = 100 boxes
```

Tum continuously boxes rakhte ja rahe ho:

```text
100 boxes → Room full
101st box → Space nahi hai ❌
```

Java me:

```text
Heap full
   ↓
New object ke liye space nahi
   ↓
OutOfMemoryError
```

---

### Interview me directly bolo:

> **OutOfMemoryError occurs when the JVM cannot allocate enough memory for new objects. It can happen because of excessive object creation, memory leaks, large objects, or insufficient heap size.**

### 🧠 Yaad rakho:

**Heap full + new object ke liye space nahi = `OutOfMemoryError`**

