Koi problem nahi 👍 Isko bahut simple way me samjho.

# Q23. `yield` kya hai Java me?

`yield` ka use **switch expression ke andar value return karne ke liye** hota hai.

### Pehle normal switch dekho

```java
int day = 2;

String result;

switch (day) {
    case 1:
        result = "Monday";
        break;

    case 2:
        result = "Tuesday";
        break;

    default:
        result = "Invalid";
}
```

Yahan hum `result` variable me value assign kar rahe hain.

---

## Java me switch expression

Ab `switch` khud **value return** kar sakta hai:

```java
int day = 2;

String result = switch (day) {

    case 1 -> "Monday";

    case 2 -> "Tuesday";

    default -> "Invalid";
};
```

Yahan:

```text
switch(day)
    ↓
case 2
    ↓
"Tuesday"
    ↓
result
```

### Lekin `yield` kab chahiye?

Jab case ke andar **multiple statements** hain.

Example:

```java
int day = 2;

String result = switch (day) {

    case 1 -> "Monday";

    case 2 -> {
        System.out.println("Today is day 2");

        String name = "Tuesday";

        yield name;
    }

    default -> "Invalid";
};
```

Yahan:

```java
yield name;
```

ka matlab hai:

> **Is switch case se ye value return karo.**

So:

```text
case 2
   ↓
multiple statements
   ↓
yield "Tuesday"
   ↓
result = "Tuesday"
```

---

# `return` vs `yield`

Ye important hai.

### `return`

Method se value return karta hai:

```java
return value;
```

### `yield`

**Switch expression ke case/block se value return karta hai:**

```java
yield value;
```

---

## 🧠 Ekdum simple trick

```text
return → method se value bahar

yield → switch expression se value bahar
```

### Interview me directly bolo:

> **`yield` is used inside a switch expression to return a value from a case block, especially when the case contains multiple statements.**

### Example yaad rakho:

```java
String result = switch (day) {

    case 1 -> "Monday";

    case 2 -> {
        String value = "Tuesday";
        yield value;
    }

    default -> "Invalid";
};
```

**Bas itna yaad rakho:**

> **`yield` = switch case ke block se value return karo.**

