# KARAT ACTUAL QUESTION — Shipping Cost

### Q. Products ship karne hain. Local shipping me product ke size ke according cost calculate hota hai, while internal shipping me flat cost charge hota hai. Interviewer ne code ki mistake aur improvement poocha.

---

## 1. Problem ko simple language me samjho

Do shipping types hain:

### Local Shipping

Cost product ke **size** par depend karega.

```text
Small  → ₹50
Medium → ₹100
Large  → ₹200
```

### Internal Shipping

Size kuch bhi ho, **flat cost**:

```text
Any size → ₹100
```

---

# 2. Interviewer actually kya check kar raha hai?

Sirf calculation nahi.

Wo dekh raha hai:

> **Kya tum code me design problem identify kar sakte ho aur usko better design me convert kar sakte ho?**

Agar code aisa hai:

```java
if (shippingType.equals("LOCAL")) {
    // size based calculation
} else if (shippingType.equals("INTERNAL")) {
    // flat cost
}
```

to problem ho sakti hai.

Kal new shipping type aaya:

```text
International
Express
SameDay
```

to existing class me aur `if-else` add karna padega.

```text
LOCAL
   ↓
INTERNAL
   ↓
INTERNATIONAL
   ↓
EXPRESS
   ↓
SAME_DAY
```

Ye code ko difficult to maintain bana deta hai.

---

# 3. Better Design — Strategy Pattern

Yahan **Strategy Pattern** use kar sakte hain.

Common interface:

```java
public interface ShippingStrategy {

    double calculateCost(Product product);
}
```

### Local Shipping

```java
public class LocalShipping implements ShippingStrategy {

    @Override
    public double calculateCost(Product product) {

        return product.getSize() * 10;
    }
}
```

### Internal Shipping

```java
public class InternalShipping implements ShippingStrategy {

    @Override
    public double calculateCost(Product product) {

        return 100;
    }
}
```

Ab main shipping service:

```java
public class ShippingService {

    private final ShippingStrategy strategy;

    public ShippingService(ShippingStrategy strategy) {
        this.strategy = strategy;
    }

    public double calculateShippingCost(Product product) {
        return strategy.calculateCost(product);
    }
}
```

Use:

```java
Product product = new Product(10);

ShippingService local =
        new ShippingService(new LocalShipping());

System.out.println(
    local.calculateShippingCost(product)
);
```

Internal:

```java
ShippingService internal =
        new ShippingService(new InternalShipping());

System.out.println(
    internal.calculateShippingCost(product)
);
```

---

# 4. Is design ka benefit

Ab kal **International Shipping** add karna ho:

```java
public class InternationalShipping
        implements ShippingStrategy {

    @Override
    public double calculateCost(Product product) {
        return product.getSize() * 50;
    }
}
```

Bas new strategy add ki.

`ShippingService` ko change karne ki zarurat nahi. ✅

---

# 🎯 Karat me directly bolna

> **The main design issue is that shipping logic is tightly coupled with the shipping type. If we use multiple if-else conditions, adding a new shipping type requires modifying existing code. I would separate each shipping algorithm using a common ShippingStrategy interface and implement LocalShipping and InternalShipping separately. This follows the Strategy Pattern and makes the code easier to extend and maintain.**

### 🧠 Yaad rakhna:

```text
Different calculation/algorithm
          ↓
Strategy Pattern
          ↓
One common interface
          ↓
Different implementations
```

### Important

**Agar tumhare paas interviewer ka actual code hai**, woh bhi bhej dena. Is question me **exact mistake** code dekhkar identify karna zyada important hai, kyunki abhi tumne scenario bataya hai, actual code nahi.

