## 🎯 Interview Answer

> **"The Test Pyramid recommends having more fast and isolated unit tests, fewer integration tests, and a smaller number of end-to-end tests. In Spring Boot, I would use unit tests for business logic, integration tests to verify interactions between components and the database, and end-to-end tests for critical complete user journeys. This gives good coverage while keeping the test suite fast and maintainable."**

