## 🔥 KARAT ACTUAL QUESTION — Q30

### **What are readiness and liveness probes in Kubernetes?**

Ye question basically pooch raha hai:

> **Kubernetes ko kaise pata chalega ki application alive hai aur traffic lene ke liye ready hai?**

---

## 1️⃣ Liveness Probe

**Liveness = Application zinda hai ya nahi?**

Suppose Spring Boot application hang ho gayi:

```text
Spring Boot
     ↓
Application stuck ❌
```

Container technically running hai, but application properly kaam nahi kar rahi.

Kubernetes liveness probe check karega:

```text
Liveness check
      ↓
Healthy? ✅ → kuch nahi karega

Unhealthy? ❌
      ↓
Container restart
```

Example:

```yaml
livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health
    port: 8080
  initialDelaySeconds: 30
  periodSeconds: 10
```

---

# 2️⃣ Readiness Probe

**Readiness = Application traffic lene ke liye ready hai ya nahi?**

Suppose application start ho rahi hai:

```text
Application starting...
      ↓
DB connection
      ↓
Loading configuration
      ↓
Loading cache
      ↓
Ready ✅
```

Jab tak ready nahi hai, Kubernetes usko traffic nahi bhejega.

```text
Readiness check
      ↓
Ready? ❌
      ↓
No traffic

Ready? ✅
      ↓
Traffic allowed
```

Example:

```yaml
readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health/readiness
    port: 8080
  initialDelaySeconds: 20
  periodSeconds: 5
```

---

# 🔥 Main Difference

| Probe         | Question                            | Failure par                    |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| **Liveness**  | App alive hai?                      | Container restart ho sakta hai |
| **Readiness** | App traffic lene ke liye ready hai? | Traffic temporarily stop       |

### Real example

```text
             Spring Boot Pod
                   |
          ┌────────┴────────┐
          ↓                 ↓
     Liveness            Readiness
     "Alive?"             "Ready?"
          ↓                 ↓
      Restart            No traffic
      if dead             if not ready
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick

> **Live = Restart**
> **Ready = Traffic**

### 🎯 Interview Answer

> "Liveness probe checks whether the application is still alive and functioning; if it fails, Kubernetes can restart the container. Readiness probe checks whether the application is ready to receive traffic; if it fails, Kubernetes removes the pod from service endpoints but does not necessarily restart it."

