## 🔥 KARAT ACTUAL QUESTION — Q32

### **When would you use Strategy Pattern vs Template Method Pattern in Spring?**

Dono ka purpose hai **code ko reusable aur maintainable banana**, but approach different hai.

---

# 1️⃣ Strategy Pattern

### Simple meaning:

> **Same kaam karne ke multiple ways hain, aur mujhe runtime par choose karna hai → Strategy.**

Example: Payment

```text id="jv0p5u"
Payment
 ├── CreditCardPayment
 ├── UpiPayment
 └── NetBankingPayment
```

Interface:

```java
public interface PaymentStrategy {
    void pay(double amount);
}
```

Implementations:

```java
@Component
public class UpiPayment implements PaymentStrategy {

    public void pay(double amount) {
        System.out.println("UPI payment: " + amount);
    }
}
```

```java
@Component
public class CardPayment implements PaymentStrategy {

    public void pay(double amount) {
        System.out.println("Card payment: " + amount);
    }
}
```

Then application requirement ke according strategy choose kar sakte ho.

### Main idea:

```text
Strategy A
Strategy B
Strategy C
    ↓
Choose one
```

---

# 2️⃣ Template Method Pattern

Yahan situation different hai.

> **Process/steps same hain, but kuch steps subclasses mein different hain → Template Method.**

Example: Loan processing.

Har loan mein process:

```text id="q3x8i9"
1. Validate application
2. Check eligibility
3. Calculate interest
4. Approve
```

Overall flow same hai, but kuch step implementation different ho sakti hai.

```java
public abstract class LoanProcessor {

    public final void process() {
        validate();
        checkEligibility();
        calculateInterest();
        approve();
    }

    abstract void checkEligibility();
    abstract void calculateInterest();

    void validate() {
        System.out.println("Common validation");
    }

    void approve() {
        System.out.println("Loan approved");
    }
}
```

Different loan types:

```text id="t7y4uk"
LoanProcessor
      |
 ┌────┴─────┐
 ↓          ↓
HomeLoan   PersonalLoan
```

`process()` ka flow same rahega.

---

# 🔥 Main Difference

| Strategy                                   | Template Method                     |
| ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| Multiple algorithms/approaches             | Same overall algorithm/process      |
| Composition                                | Inheritance                         |
| Runtime par strategy change kar sakte hain | Parent class flow control karti hai |
| Interface commonly used                    | Abstract class commonly used        |

### Easy Example

**Strategy:**

> "Payment kaise karna hai?"

```text
UPI / Card / NetBanking
```

**Template:**

> "Loan process ka flow kya hai?"

```text
Validate
 → Eligibility
 → Calculate
 → Approve
```

Flow same hai, kuch steps implementation different.

---

## 🧠 Memory Trick

> **Strategy = WHAT WAY?**
> **Template = WHAT STEPS?**

### 🎯 Interview Answer

> "I use Strategy Pattern when I have multiple interchangeable algorithms or behaviors and need to select one, often at runtime. I use Template Method when the overall workflow is fixed but some individual steps need different implementations. Strategy generally favors composition, while Template Method uses inheritance."

**Spring mein Strategy Pattern** dependency injection ke saath bahut commonly implement hota hai, especially jab multiple implementations of the same interface available hon.

