## 🔥 Q54. What is the difference between `SecurityFilterChain` and `WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter`?

Ye tumhare image wale **Q54** ka question hai.

### 1️⃣ `WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter`

Purane Spring Security versions mein security configuration ke liye use hota tha:

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig
        extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter {

    @Override
    protected void configure(HttpSecurity http)
            throws Exception {

        http
            .authorizeRequests()
            .antMatchers("/public/**").permitAll()
            .anyRequest().authenticated();
    }
}
```

Yaani:

```text
WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter
        ↓
extend class
        ↓
override configure()
        ↓
security configuration
```

**Important:** Newer Spring Security mein `WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter` deprecated/removed approach hai. Modern Spring Security mein bean-based configuration preferred hai.

---

# 2️⃣ `SecurityFilterChain`

Modern Spring Security mein hum `SecurityFilterChain` bean define karte hain:

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    SecurityFilterChain securityFilterChain(HttpSecurity http)
            throws Exception {

        http
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .requestMatchers("/public/**").permitAll()
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            );

        return http.build();
    }
}
```

Flow:

```text
Request
   ↓
Spring Security Filters
   ↓
SecurityFilterChain
   ↓
Authentication / Authorization
   ↓
Controller
```

---

# 🔥 Main Difference

| `WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter` | `SecurityFilterChain`            |
| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------- |
| Old approach                   | Modern approach                  |
| Class extend karni padti thi   | Bean define karte hain           |
| `configure()` override         | `SecurityFilterChain` bean       |
| Deprecated approach            | Recommended modern configuration |

### 🧠 Easy Trick

```text
OLD
WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter
       ↓
extends + override

NEW
SecurityFilterChain
       ↓
@Bean
```

### 🎯 Interview Answer

> **"`WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter` was the traditional way of configuring Spring Security by extending a base class and overriding configuration methods. It has been deprecated and the modern approach is to define a `SecurityFilterChain` bean, which provides more explicit and flexible configuration."**

